    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">1. Services and Scheduling</h2>
        <p>You book appointments through the website. Times that are already taken are not offered, and a booking is confirmed once you receive confirmation from the booking system. Services are performed on-site at your location or remotely, as agreed when you book.</p>
        <p>Please arrive ready: have the device, drives, passwords, and any equipment you want worked on available at the appointment. If I cannot do the work because something is missing, locked, or not as described, I may need to reschedule.</p>
        <p><strong>Safe Environment:</strong> I reserve the right to refuse service or terminate an on-site appointment immediately if the environment is unsafe, unsanitary, or hostile. If an appointment is terminated for these reasons, the $30 minimum charge and any travel fee still apply.</p>
        <p>If you need to cancel or reschedule, please give at least 24 hours of notice. There is no cancellation fee. If you repeatedly miss appointments without notice, I may decline future bookings.</p>
        <p>The session times shown for each service are estimates based on experience. Some situations may take longer and others may take less time, depending on the circumstances and the condition of your equipment.</p>
        <p>Because times are estimates and can vary, I will see as many customers as I can on the day they schedule their appointment. If I am unable to make it on that day, I will contact you to arrange another day.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">2. Pricing and Payment</h2>
        <p>Each service on the website has a flat price in US dollars. That price is what you pay for the service, whether it is done on-site or remotely, and it covers the time listed for that service. If a session needs to run past that time, the extra time is billed at $50 per hour in 15-minute increments. I will let you know before continuing past the listed time. The price shown when you book is the price for that booking, even if prices change later.</p>
        <p>Work that is not one of the listed services is billed hourly. The first hour is $65 on-site or $55 remote, then $50 per hour in 15-minute increments. Work under one hour is $1 per minute with a 30-minute minimum ($30).</p>
        <p>There is no travel fee within 25 miles of my home base, ZIP code 32259-3268, measured one way by driving distance. Beyond that, the fee is $1.50 for each mile past 25 miles. It is based on the one-way driving distance from my home base to your address, no matter what order my appointments fall in that day. Any travel fee is part of the plan and cost I give you before work begins.</p>
        <p>There is no extra charge for same-day appointments or after-hours appointments.</p>
        <p>You supply all hardware and parts. I charge for labor only. I am not responsible for the choice, compatibility, or condition of hardware you supply.</p>
        <p>Payment is due after the appointment, and I take payments through Stripe. At the end of your visit you can pay by tapping a credit or debit card, or a mobile wallet such as Apple Pay or Google Pay, on my phone. If you would rather not pay that way, or your card or phone cannot tap to pay, I will send a secure payment link to the email address on your appointment. Payment through the link is expected within 7 days of the date it is sent. After 7 days, a late fee of $4 per day applies until the balance is paid, but late fees never total more than 25% of the original amount owed. Fees for completed work are non-refundable, except where these terms say otherwise.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">3. Your Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>You are responsible for backing up your data before any work begins. Working on computers, drives, and software always carries some risk of data loss. I may offer to make a copy of your files as part of a service, but a copy made by me does not replace your own backup, and I do not guarantee that it will be complete.</p>
        <p>By booking, you confirm that you own the devices and data involved, or that the owner has given you permission to have them worked on.</p>
        <p>Please describe the problem as accurately as you can, including anything that happened beforehand, such as drops, spills, power loss, recent updates, or earlier repair attempts. Missing details can change what is possible and how long it takes.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for providing the passwords, encryption keys, and account access needed for the work. I cannot bypass a password, disk encryption, or account lock that you are unable to unlock yourself.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for having valid licenses for any software you ask me to install. I do not install pirated or unlicensed software.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">4. Data Recovery and Failing Drives</h2>
        <p>Data recovery is never guaranteed. A drive that is failing, damaged, or accidentally formatted can lose more data, or stop working entirely, at any moment. That can happen while I evaluate it, copy it, or recover files from it, and even reading a failing drive can make it worse.</p>
        <p>If a drive or device fails further, becomes unreadable, or loses data while I am evaluating or recovering it, I am not responsible and cannot be held liable for that failure, for the loss of data that could otherwise have been recovered, or for any resulting costs. By approving an evaluation or a recovery, you accept this risk.</p>
        <p>I take steps to lower the risk, such as copying a drive's readable data to an image first and working from the copy whenever possible. These steps reduce the risk but do not remove it.</p>
        <p>The 30-minute Data Recovery Evaluation checks the drive's health and what looks recoverable before you decide to continue. Its findings are an estimate, not a promise of the final result.</p>
        <p>Fees work like this:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>If you decide not to continue after the evaluation, you pay the evaluation fee only.</li>
            <li>If you approve a full recovery, you pay the full recovery price. The evaluation fee is not added on top.</li>
            <li>If I cannot recover any usable files, you pay the evaluation fee only.</li>
            <li>If I recover some but not all of your data, the full recovery price still applies, because the result depends on the condition of the drive.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Recovered files may be incomplete or damaged. When files are recovered by scanning rather than from the drive's folder structure, file names and folders are often lost. I will tell you what to expect before you approve the recovery.</p>
        <p>Recovered files are copied to a drive you provide, so please have one with enough free space ready.</p>
        <p>Some drives are not detected, click, grind, or are physically damaged. They need a specialized clean-room lab, which I do not offer. If I find this, I will stop and tell you so I do not cause more damage. Any lab you choose is a separate business, and I am not responsible for its work, prices, or results. The only thing I will provide is a suggested business or businesses to take to for the work.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">5. Other Services</h2>
        <p><strong>Malware and scam cleanup.</strong> I work to remove malicious software and unauthorized access, but I cannot guarantee that every threat is gone or that you will not be infected again. After a scam, I cannot recover money you have sent or reverse a payment. Contact your bank, card company, or the authorities as soon as you can.</p>
        <p><strong>Passwords and two-step verification.</strong> You create and keep your own master password, recovery codes, and backup codes. I do not keep copies and cannot recover them for you. Losing them can lock you out of an account permanently.</p>
        <p><strong>Secure drive sanitization.</strong> Wiping a drive is permanent and cannot be undone. Before I start, you confirm which drives to erase and that you have copies of anything you want to keep. I am not responsible for data erased from a drive you asked me to wipe. I follow accepted industry methods, but no method can guarantee a complete wipe of every drive, especially failing or damaged ones and some solid-state drives. If the data is extremely sensitive, physical destruction of the drive is safer.</p>
        <p><strong>Reinstalls, migrations, cloning, and operating system changes.</strong> These services erase or move large amounts of data. Some programs, files, or settings may not transfer, and some software does not run on every operating system, including Linux. Keep your own backup of anything that matters.</p>
        <p><strong>Hardware installation.</strong> Opening a device or installing parts can affect a manufacturer's warranty, and you accept that. I install the parts you supply but do not guarantee them. Older or worn equipment can fail on its own, and I am not responsible for failures that were already developing before I started or that are unrelated to my work.</p>
        <p><strong>Abandoned Hardware:</strong> If equipment is left unpaid or uncollected for 30 days after I send you written notice by email that it is ready, it becomes the property of England Technologies LLC. Any data on it will be securely erased before it is reused, recycled, or disposed of.</p>
        <p><strong>Networking.</strong> I change router and network settings only as needed for the service. I am not responsible for internet provider outages, equipment limits, or problems on the provider's side. I will give you any new network names and passwords I set up.</p>
    </div></div>
