        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">6. Remote Sessions</h2>
        <p>Remote sessions only happen at a time we have agreed on, and only with your permission. You start the connection yourself, and you can end it at any moment. I will never contact you out of the blue and ask for remote access to your computer. If someone claiming to be me does, it is not me.</p>
        <p>During a session I access only what the work requires. Please stay near your device so you can see what is being done and answer questions. When the session ends, I remove any remote-access software I installed for it, or tell you how to remove it.</p>
        <p>A remote session needs a working internet connection on your end. I am not responsible for dropped connections, slow connections, or problems caused by your internet provider or equipment. If a problem cannot be fixed remotely, I will tell you and we can arrange an on-site visit.</p>
